# Unit01
# 领域: 考研
# 学科: 英语词汇
# 来源: 2024红宝书考研英语词汇
# 描述: 必考词Unit01核心词汇

abandon/əˈbændən/放弃；抛弃/The plan was abandoned due to lack of funds.
abstract/ˈæbstrækt/抽象的；摘要/Please write an abstract for your paper.
absurd/əbˈsɜːrd/荒谬的/The idea sounds absurd but it might work.
abundance/əˈbʌndəns/丰富；充裕/The region has an abundance of natural resources.
accelerate/əkˈseləreɪt/加速/The government aims to accelerate economic growth.
access/ˈækses/进入；通道/Everyone should have access to quality education.
accommodate/əˈkɑːmədeɪt/容纳；适应/The hotel can accommodate up to 300 guests.
accompany/əˈkʌmpəni/陪伴/Lightning is often accompanied by thunder.
accomplish/əˈkɑːmplɪʃ/完成/She accomplished her mission successfully.
accumulate/əˈkjuːmjəleɪt/积累/He accumulated vast experience over the years.
accurate/ˈækjərət/准确的/The report provides an accurate description of the event.
accuse/əˈkjuːz/指控/He was accused of fraud.
acknowledge/əkˈnɑːlɪdʒ/承认/She acknowledged that she had made an error.
acquire/əˈkwaɪər/获得/He acquired a taste for classical music.
adapt/əˈdæpt/适应；改编/Animals must adapt to changing environments.
adequate/ˈædɪkwət/足够的/The funding is adequate for the project.
advocate/ˈædvəkeɪt/提倡/She advocates for equal rights for women.
affect/əˈfekt/影响/The policy will directly affect small businesses.
aggressive/əˈɡresɪv/有进取心的/She has an aggressive approach to business.
alert/əˈlɜːrt/警觉的/Drivers should be alert to road conditions.
alien/ˈeɪliən/外星人的/The concept is alien to our culture.
allocate/ˈæləkeɪt/分配/The government allocated funds for education.
alter/ˈɔːltər/改变/They altered the plan slightly.
alternative/ɔːlˈtɜːrnətɪv/替代的/We need to find an alternative energy source.
ambiguous/æmˈbɪɡjuəs/模糊的/The statement is ambiguous and open to interpretation.
amend/əˈmend/修正/The law was amended to include new provisions.
analogy/əˈnælədʒi/类比/He drew an analogy between the brain and a computer.
analyze/ˈænəlaɪz/分析/We need to analyze the data more carefully.
anticipate/ænˈtɪsɪpeɪt/预料/We anticipate a rise in demand next quarter.
apparent/əˈpærənt/明显的/It was apparent that the plan had failed.
appeal/əˈpiːl/呼吁；上诉/She appealed to the public for donations.
applicable/əˈplɪkəbl/适用的/This rule is applicable to all students.
appoint/əˈpɔɪnt/任命/He was appointed as the new director.
appraisal/əˈpreɪzl/评估/The appraisal of the property was very thorough.
appreciate/əˈpriːʃieɪt/感激；增值/I appreciate your generous help.
approach/əˈproʊtʃ/方法；接近/We need a new approach to solve this problem.
appropriate/əˈproʊpriət/适当的/This is not an appropriate time for discussion.
approve/əˈpruːv/批准/The board approved the new budget.
arbitrary/ˈɑːrbrɪteri/任意的/The decision seemed completely arbitrary.
arise/əˈraɪz/出现/New challenges may arise during the project.
assert/əˈsɜːrt/断言/She asserted her innocence throughout the trial.
assess/əˈses/评估/We need to assess the risks involved.
assign/əˈsaɪn/分配/She was assigned to lead the team.
assume/əˈsuːm/假设/Don't assume that everyone agrees with you.
assure/əˈʃʊr/保证/I can assure you of the quality of our products.
attach/əˈtætʃ/附上；重视/She attaches great importance to education.
attain/əˈteɪn/达到/She attained the highest score in the exam.
attribute/əˈtrɪbjuːt/归因于/He attributed his success to hard work.
authentic/ɔːˈθentɪk/真实的/This is an authentic painting from the 18th century.
